# database.sqlite is no longer tracked and is no longer the deployed content
# store. Production reads and writes a hosted Postgres database (Neon), so
# /admin saves directly and the public page reflects the change immediately —
# no commit, no redeploy.
#
# It was committed while Vercel served it read-only; its content was ported into
# Postgres by `php artisan portfolio:port-to-pgsql` and it is now ignored, so a
# stale local copy can never be mistaken for production data. Editing a local
# SQLite file has no effect on the deployed site.
#
# Production requires DB_CONNECTION=pgsql plus DB_URL; SESSION_DRIVER and
# CACHE_STORE are on the `database` driver, which the old read-only SQLite setup
# could not support.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# Local pre-migration backups, not source.
*.sqlite.bak
